# GoThru 3D — Next.js Frontend Auth & Persistence Implementation Plan (v2)

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Wire auth, session management, and project persistence into the existing Next.js frontend using NextAuth v5 and Server Actions — no proxy rewrites, no client-side fetches to the Go service.

**Architecture:** NextAuth v5 (Auth.js) manages the session. On login, its credentials provider calls Go `/v1/auth/login` server-to-server and stores the returned JWT as `accessToken` in the encrypted NextAuth session cookie. All Go API calls are Server Actions (server → server with `Authorization: Bearer`). File upload is the only browser-initiated API call, routed through a Next.js Route Handler. No `next.config.ts` proxy rewrites. No `src/lib/api.ts` helper (replaced by Server Actions). Middleware uses NextAuth's `auth` wrapper — reads the NextAuth session cookie to determine login state and `emailVerified` status.

**Tech Stack:** Next.js 16 · NextAuth v5 (next-auth@5) · React 19 · TypeScript 5 · Zustand 5

## Global Constraints

- No `next.config.ts` proxy rewrites — all Go calls are server-to-server
- No `src/lib/api.ts` / `apiFetch` / `apiJSON` — replaced by Server Actions
- No `gf_verified` cookie — `session.user.emailVerified` from NextAuth session is the gate
- No `jose` JWT library in middleware — NextAuth `auth()` handles session decoding
- All routes to Go use `process.env.GOTHRU_API_URL` (never hardcoded)
- Go routes: `/v1/auth/*`, `/v1/projects/*`, `/v1/upload`, `/v1/files`, `/v1/reset`
- Server Actions use `"use server"` directive and call Go with `Authorization: Bearer ${session.accessToken}`
- File upload via `src/app/api/upload/route.ts` — browser → Next.js → Go (Bearer token added server-side)
- `pnpm` package manager; typecheck with `npx tsc --noEmit` before declaring done
- Env: `NEXTAUTH_URL`, `NEXTAUTH_SECRET`, `GOTHRU_API_URL`
- No source file may exceed 500 lines — if a file grows beyond this during implementation, split it into focused sub-files before committing (e.g. `src/actions/auth-session.ts` + `src/actions/auth-password.ts`); each sub-file must export only its own functions and import from the others if needed

