## Self-Review Checklist

- [x] No `next.config.ts` proxy rewrites for `/api/v1/*`
- [x] No `src/lib/api.ts` / `apiFetch` / `apiJSON` — replaced by Server Actions
- [x] No `gf_verified` cookie checks — `session.user.emailVerified` used everywhere
- [x] No `jose` or manual JWT decoding in middleware — NextAuth `auth()` handles it
- [x] All Go calls in Server Actions use `Authorization: Bearer ${session.accessToken}`
- [x] File upload stays as browser `fetch` to `/api/upload` Route Handler (file bytes cannot pass through Server Actions)
- [x] `verifyEmailAction` returns `{verified: true}` from Go (not a redirect); client calls `session.update()` next
- [x] `jwt` callback handles `trigger === "update"` — calls Go `/v1/auth/me` to get latest `emailVerified`
- [x] `logoutAction` calls `signOut({ redirect: false })` — caller handles redirect
- [x] Middleware matcher covers `/start/:path*`, `/editor/:path*`, `/dashboard/:path*` only
- [x] `GOTHRU_API_URL` used throughout — never hardcoded
- [x] `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` in `.env.local` — never committed
- [x] TypeScript errors resolved before each commit
- [x] `src/actions/billing.ts` — all 3 actions use `"use server"`, read `GOTHRU_API_URL`, pass `Authorization: Bearer` header
- [x] `src/app/billing/page.tsx` — calls `getBillingStatus` on mount; `handleSubscribe` / `handleManage` redirect via `window.location.href`
- [x] Success and cancel pages exist at `/billing/success` and `/billing/cancel` matching Stripe redirect URLs
- [x] No Stripe client-side library (`@stripe/stripe-js`) — Stripe Hosted Checkout means only the redirect URL is needed
